WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.220
It's the Japanese Featherweight Title Match.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:07.480
The challenger, Sanada Kazuki, rushes towards the champion, Makunouchi Ippo!

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.490
The champion uses a cross-arm block!

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.910
The challenger cuts loose with the Hien!

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.620
And this...

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.540
Is it the Champion's finishing blow, the Dempsey Roll!?

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.170
Sanada stops it by charging into him!

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.590
But he's struck with a liver blow!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.090
The challenger is buckling over in pain!

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:36.840
And launched from that position...

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.010
is the Gazelle Punch!

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.720
Explosive!

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.140
Now, here comes the Dempsey Roll!

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.940
The champion launches into a fearsome rush, intent on his first title defense!

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.940
He keeps going!

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.320
Whoa!

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.700
The Dempsey Roll has stopped!

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.000
The champion's knees buckle!

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.210
Has he run out of strength!?

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.050
With the champion stopped, Sanada takes aim!

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.140
Whoa!

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.560
The challenger falls!

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.670
An unexpected ending!

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.190
Makunouchi Ippo wins; it is a miraculous win in his first title defense!

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.720
Mom, I'll carry that one.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.710
Really?

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.100
Okay, take care of it.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.460
Good morning!

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:53.340
Okay, I'll take you to the boat, so just follow me, please!

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.050
Worms.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:56.980
Check!

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.330
Tackle box.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.230
Check!

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.690
All right, you carry that.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.480
Okay.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.620
Thanks, Champion.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:32.510
U-Umezawa-kun, cut out that "Champion" stuff.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.430
It's nothing to be embarrassed about.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.660
You did win your first title defense.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.060
Ippo-kun, you're a fine Japanese Featherweight Champion.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.210
Show some pride!

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.270
That's right!

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.420
O-Okay...

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:56.050
All right, we're heading out, Champion!

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.910
Have a safe trip!

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.250
Kimura, Aoki, three sets left!

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.280
Keep it up!

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.050
Right!

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:33.180
Things have been heating up at the Kamogawa Boxing Gym lately.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.490
Takamura-kun is still undefeated heading into the match that will be a stepping stone to his world title fight.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:48.620
And...

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.720
What's wrong, kid? Put some weight into it!

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:52.550
Right!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.300
Ippo-kun succeeded in his first title defense as the Japanese Featherweight Champion.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:04.390
There's no sign of the boy who used to get picked on when he first came to this gym.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.640
All right, kid! Finish it!

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:07.690
Right!

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.190
Good work out there today!

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.740
I'm heading home!

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.920
Ippo-kun has the prestige of being the champion now.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.900
And Takamura has that match before his world title fight coming up soon too.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.740
Aoki and Kimura are both motivated to work harder because of their influence.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.130
What a bunch of naive nonsense.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.430
The kid, prestigious?

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.870
Not yet, he's not.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.190
He's a far cry from acting like a real champion.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.330
The kid, Aoki, Kimura...

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.670
They all need to aim higher.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:49.000
They all have the potential of reaching much greater glory than they could ever imagine.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.060
Coach...

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.060
Yagi-chan, Shinoda-kun,

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.890
we need to keep whipping them into shape!

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:56.690
I'm counting on you!

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.400
Right!

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.660
<i>That's right.</i>

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.210
<i>Aim higher,</i>

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.460
<i>and reach that goal.</i>

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:11.420
<i>If possible, while there's still some light left in these old eyes.</i>

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.000
Boom! Boom!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.830
My punches are dynamite!

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:17.840
Hey, Ippo!

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.720
How have things been with Kumi-chan lately?

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.380
<i>Makunouchi-san!</i>

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.730
N-Nothing special...

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.950
Tomiko was asking about you two!

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.100
Tomiko-san?

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.110
<i>Masaru!</i>

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.360
Tomiko...

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.740
Anyway, you won your title defense, so don't you think it's about time!?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.640
T-Time?

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.010
Yeah, man!

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:54.620
<i>Kumi-san...</i>

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:55.860
<i>Yes?</i>

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:58.880
<i>I...</i>

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:01.880
<i>want to be your champion belt.</i>

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.090
<i>Makunouchi-san... {jama: added}</i>

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.690
<i>I want to feel you wrapped around me!</i>

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:10.750
Tighter!

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.570
Here, right here!?

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.610
Harder!

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.340
Here, like this!?

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:17.600
What are you doing?

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.260
<i>But... the right time, huh?</i>

00:06:20.260 --> 00:06:24.030
<i>Maybe it's a good time, like Aoki-san says, to share my feelings.</i>

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.760
You sure about that?

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.620
If you make a move on Kumi-chan, her sweet older brother will have something to say about it.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:34.210
<i>Makunouchi...</i>

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.040
<i>I'll kill you!</i>

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:41.540
<i>Die!</i>

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.930
Fool, I'm just kidding!

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.110
And even if her sweet older brother shows up,

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:52.040
just KO him with your megaton punch!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:54.140
I don't have a megaton punch.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.120
Oh yeah, you do...

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.650
You got it right here!

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:01.190
The megaton punch of the world heavyweight champion!

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:04.240
This thing could take care of Mashiba and Kumi-chan with one blow!

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.430
Stop it!

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:08.200
Takamura-san, Aoki-san!

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:11.560
Geez, could you please cut it out?

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.040
If you're a real man, you gotta show her what you've got!

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:14.910
Huh?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.500
Kimura-san, are you going somewhere?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.260
Yeah,

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:22.870
I thought I'd do a little sparring with Miyata.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:24.960
With Miyata-kun!?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.550
That's right!

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.310
Miyata-kun's OPBF, Oriental Pacific
 Boxing Federation, title match is soon!

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:35.890
I'm looking forward to it!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:41.080
You think you can worry about that sort of thing when you're still being challenged for your belt at the national level?

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:45.990
At least show some guts and say something about how you're gonna take the OPBF belt!

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.370
N-No,

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.110
there's no way I could do that.

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.110
Wimp,

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.620
do you wanna beat Miyata or not!?

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.810
I-I'd like to someday, but...

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.670
Miyata-kun is really strong...

00:07:58.670 --> 00:07:59.870
and cool.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:04.380
Hey, are you after both Kumi-chan and Miyata?

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:06.260
That's not it!

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:10.890
I just look up to Miyata-kun as a boxer, that's all!

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:13.760
All right, I'm taking off!

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.010
Okay! Good luck!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.850
Say hi to Miyata-kun for me!

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.430
Wanpo, did you come to get me?

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.520
This is where it all started...

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.770
Meeting Takamura-san, starting boxing...

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.150
and then suddenly sparring with Miyata-kun.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:14.570
I was KO'd by a counter...

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.150
I could barely touch him.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.410
But...

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.280
in our second spar...

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.950
<i>Ippo wins!</i>

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.210
<i>As of now, it's tied 1-1.</i>

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.040
<i>We'll settle this in the pro ring.</i>

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.590
<i>The Eastern Japan Rookie Tournament Finals.</i>

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.090
<i>I'll be waiting for you there!</i>

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.550
<i>But Miyata-kun was...</i>

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.560
<i>I won the Rookie King Tournament,</i>

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.940
<i>but I never got to fight Miyata-kun.</i>

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.440
<i>I'll be leaving Japan for a while.</i>

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:59.320
<i>I plan on traveling to Korea and Thailand to train.</i>

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.950
<i>Amazing! How long will you be overseas?</i>

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.790
<i>The All-Japan Rookie King, huh?</i>

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.880
<i>It seems that the gap between us has grown quite a bit in such a short time.</i>

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:18.260
<i>I'll be back... when that gap is filled.</i>

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.840
And Miyata-kun came back!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:25.100
He got really, really strong and came back!

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.140
I'm sure he can become the OPBF Champion!

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.690
Miyata-kun can do it! Right, Wanpo!?

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.780
What the hell, that's the third down!

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.280
Quit holding back!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:43.910
Holding back?

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.120
Is that what it seems like?

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.950
W-Well, I mean...

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.250
That's enough sparring!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.000
Dad...

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.380
There's only a week until the match.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.670
We'll be switching to light practice for the remainder of the time!

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:55.800
I-I can still-

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.630
Do you want to get injured and ruin your title match?

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:04.680
I'll go get changed.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.940
I guess I have gotten stronger after all.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:14.400
I came to help Miyata build his confidence, but it ended up working the other way around.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:18.940
I-I'm just joking!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.900
I mean, he's at the peak of his exhaustion from training, right!?

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:24.700
If he was fighting seriously, I'd have been beaten!

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.740
He was quite serious.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:30.910
That was Ichiro's full featherweight power.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:35.920
<i>His weight management!?</i>

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.210
In our time overseas, we had eleven matches in one year.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.840
He fought matches at a remarkably high pace.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.550
Do you know why?

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:47.140
We couldn't have spaced them any further apart.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:51.430
While a greater interval between matches would help recover from exhaustion and damage,

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:57.190
it would have made it impossible to get his weight back down to 126 pounds for a match.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.940
It's not a simple matter of gaining or losing weight anymore.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:03.570
His physique cannot be allowed to leave the limits of the featherweight class.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:09.290
Come to think of it, Miyata's taller than me now.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:13.000
But Miyata could easily make it as a lightweight!

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.630
Hell, he might make it all the way to the world title!

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:19.710
He should stop worrying about the featherweights and go for a class where he can really...

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.300
I can't tell you how many times I've said the same thing.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:30.310
He won't lose the title match, will he?

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:36.850
The OPBF Champion, Arnie "Crocodile" Gregory,

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.110
is known for powerful left and right hooks that can shatter bones.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.110
He earned his nickname because they strike with the strength of a crocodile's jaw.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:44.240
He's undoubtedly a dangerous opponent.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:46.410
What's with that name "Crocodile!?"

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.910
Damn it, if Miyata wasn't struggling with his weight management he could easily-

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:51.830
Sorry to have worried you so much.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.790
Miyata...

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.380
In that spar,

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.210
Dad said that was my full featherweight power, right?

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.210
Let me elaborate on that.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.760
Yes, I was serious.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.470
But it was still just sparring.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:12.390
To me, weight control is like sharpening a pencil.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.810
I focus my mind by chipping away at it.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:18.480
I chip away at my body and that sharpens my concentration to a finer and finer point.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.980
The concentration that lets me see through every punch...

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.990
It's preparation so that I can pull that off in the main event.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.410
Counters, huh?

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.870
<i>When I think of how much he risks with each punch...</i>

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.580
<i>It's like wagering your own soul.</i>

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:37.870
<i>How long do you intend to fight like that?</i>

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.050
Stop, Arnie!

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.340
He knocked another one down.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:51.850
The nickname "Crocodile" isn't just for show.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:52.560
Yeah.

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:55.270
He's definitely the type of boxer that pins people down using brute strength.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:58.060
The destructive power of his left and right hooks is pretty impressive.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.690
People of the Japanese Press!

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.400
That was a sample of Arnie's prowess!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.900
We're looking for brave challengers, so please, please...

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.860
What does he mean by that?

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:13.080
Mr. Sakaguchi, the match with Miyata isn't even over yet.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.870
I came to Japan because I thought it'd be good for business.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:21.830
There're other strong boxers like Date and Makunouchi, right?

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.340
<i>He's mocking Japanese boxers.</i>

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.840
<i>This manager is full of it.</i>

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.010
Miyata Ichiro is genuinely strong!

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:29.510
W-Wait, Iimura...

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:34.100
Your boxer, who seems so proud of his brute force, is going to have circles run around him!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.930
Brute force, huh?

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.940
The Japanese Sportswriters must be blind.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:45.190
Arnie has something special for Miyata.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.280
Something special?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:53.240
It's a shame we can't show you right now, but I'm sure you'll see it during the actual match.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.450
It's called...

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.450
the Bloody Cross.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.540
Bloody Cross?

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:01.830
Yeah.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:06.000
Even coming from that arrogant manager, it genuinely sounded like a dangerous move.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.710
Bloody Cross, huh?

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:09.920
Translate it and you get a "Cross of Blood."

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:11.550
I've got it!

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:12.760
What!?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.260
You'll be wrong, but hell, give it a try!

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.060
The cross part means a counter!

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:22.770
A cross counter gets its name from when the arms cross over, right!?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:27.480
Meaning it's gotta be some badass cross counter that's so intense that it rains blood!

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:33.160
That's what I thought too, but Arnie doesn't seem like the type who uses counters.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:37.410
I don't see him being able to compete with Miyata when it comes to counters.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.660
Wrong, like I figured.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.290
Still, it's worrisome.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.540
Yeah...

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:48.960
although what bothers me is the fact that his manager is already asking for more challengers.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:52.180
I can understand being confident, but it really seems like he's underestimating him.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.430
Yeah, it's hard to swallow.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.800
If Miyata loses, you get 'im, Ippo!

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.680
There'll be no need for that.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.310
Miyata-kun won't lose.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.450
But you know, on the off-chance that-

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:06.560
There is no chance.

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:08.820
He will win.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:11.070
Please stop saying things that might jinx it.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:12.530
'Kay...

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:17.410
What do you think Miyata's chances are, Fujii-san?

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.950
Well, we didn't see the full extent of Arnie's ability, but...

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.540
his power is on par with Ippo-kun.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.830
Ippo's level?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.080
What!?

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.380
Well, that's not a big deal, right?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:31.840
Don't try and sound happy about it with that conflicted expression.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:36.510
But Miyata undoubtedly has the advantage in speed and boxing sense.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.060
I'd give Miyata 7 to 3 odds for winning.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.470
I don't like the sound of that "3."

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:45.230
Well, his manager's carefree attitude concerns me.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.560
That and...

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.520
...the Bloody Cross?

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.570
I can't get it out of my head.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.150
It's creepy.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:18.800
<i>After all that running, not a drop of sweat.</i>

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:21.890
<i>My skin feels so strange.</i>

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:33.320
<i>Wa-</i>

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.360
<i>Water...</i>

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.170
Miyata Ichiro, weighing in...

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.640
126 pounds, full limit.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:06.310
You're okay.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:17.150
You seem awfully relieved to have passed the weigh-in.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:18.900
He's a sharp one.

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:21.450
That just means the fight's already started.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.740
You're his manager, right?

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.960
Maybe instead of worrying about his next opponent, you need to be worried about your next job.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.340
When this match is over, Arnie-san won't have the belt anymore,

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.670
and I have a feeling you'll be looking for a job.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.760
What a rude challenger.

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.270
We need to teach him a lesson.

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.140
Miyata's weight management is severe.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.980
He won't last too long.

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:53.270
He seems good with counters though, so you have to be careful for that.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:55.440
No problem.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:58.360
If he goes for a counter, the match will be over.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:01.140
The Bloody Cross, huh?

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:05.370
I guess there's no need to draw it out into a long match then.

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:25.510
<i>Miyata-kun...</i>

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:35.480
<i>Thailand, Korea, the Philippines...</i>

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:40.690
<i>The reason I went on that journey was to catch up to him...</i>

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:45.200
<i>to make sure that the next time I fought him, I'd be sure to win.</i>

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:50.080
<i>I learned how to throw a counter with my entire body weight behind it...</i>

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.710
<i>the Jolt Counter.</i>

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.120
<i>But...</i>

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:57.340
<i>The winner of the Class A Tournament is Makunouchi Ippo!</i>

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.630
<i>A new champion is crowned!</i>

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.090
<i>His name is Makunouchi Ippo!</i>

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:05.590
<i>But he just kept getting further ahead...</i>

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:12.140
<i>If I take the OPBF title, I'll be in a comparable position.</i>

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:13.600
<i>That's what this match means to me.</i>

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:16.520
You're up.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.270
Right.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.150
<i>The gap between us, huh?</i>

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:22.280
<i>I may have taken the long way, but...</i>

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.410
<i>now it's time to fill that gap!</i>

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:28.780
And now...

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:32.660
the OPBF Title Match...

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:35.120
scheduled for 12 rounds will begin.
